```
Reason:
The bug occurs because when `anon_inode_getfile()` fails, the code incorrectly returns the user file descriptor (`ufd`) instead of the appropriate error code derived from `file`. This leads to misleading behavior since the caller receives a valid file descriptor instead of an error indication.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
return PTR_ERR(file);
```
Reason:
The fix changes the return statement to return `PTR_ERR(file)` when `anon_inode_getfile()` fails. This correctly provides the error code associated with the failure, ensuring that the caller receives the appropriate error indication instead of an invalid file descriptor.

